{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Moses went, etc. — I am this day.</b> This day my days and years are fulfilled — on this day I was born and on this day I die (Sotah 13)." "<b>I can no longer go out and come in.</b> One might think his strength had failed — Scripture says, ״His eye had not dimmed and his natural force had not abated.״ Rather, what is <b>I can no longer</b>? I am not permitted, for authority was taken from me and given to Joshua. Another interpretation — <b>go out and come in</b>: in matters of Torah — this teaches that the channels and springs of wisdom were sealed off from him (Sotah 13)." "<b>And YHWH said to me.</b> This is the explanation of <b>I can no longer go out and come in</b> — because YHWH <b>said to me</b>."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:59.646239517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}